    {
      "id": "claim_e2273769bc5f40ffbf5c54dca8fedade",
      "statement": "The `manifold-eval` driver creates identical initial noise for both sides: JiT reseeds a fresh on-device `torch.Generator` with the same `seed` for each side, while ControlNet draws one noise tensor once and passes that same tensor to both pipelines' `sample_latent` (with fixed source latent, real target latent, spacing, contrast labels, and Heun step count), so any before/after difference is attributable to policy weights and not sampling stochasticity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L103-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bf436815a86bdcbf640dc7b85ce20a0338676151b4414fa5836dec816fa4d2ba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L163-L222",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6672c956226841ba3570b7ec0296d8a355d3178c5a56b874daba633bb819a01c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6589aae5c36d497c9a042a2c2c18257a",
      "statement": "The `--before-dir` argument must point at a native export directory whose `model_index.json` self-describes `pipeline_class`; `_pipeline_class_of` resolves `LatentFlowPipeline` to `run_unconditional` and `ControlNetLatentFlowPipeline` to `run_paired` (no mode flag). The `--after-ckpt` is processed through `export_to_native` (the before pipeline is loaded as a probe whose components are baked in place, then discarded) and the after policy is written to `<output>/after_native`; for ControlNet only the trainable `controlnet.*` weights are baked, with the frozen base passed through verbatim.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L132-L166",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2cc98d5d9141ca9c20a625ef3c47814ebe277fea120f0b155995c31b63c12446:"
