    {
      "id": "claim_7c46e26fdb154831a4bc216c123e113d",
      "statement": "The observe-only in-training paired-fidelity monitor from ADR-0037 is shipped and active in the current tree: `PairedFidelityCallback` and its registry spec `PairedFidelitySpec` are registered by default in the supervised `manifold-train-controlnet` CLI's `default_names`; the callback runs the module's own `sample()` under `inference_mode` on a fixed paired validation subset (seeded `randperm` prefix), decodes through `VaeStage` + `LatentDecoder`, normalizes with `min_max_to_unit`, scores with `PairedFidelityMetrics`, and logs `val/psnr` / `val/ssim` via module-attached `MeanMetric` instances. The monitor never drives checkpoint selection (`monitor_metric` stays `val/x0_mae`) and never contributes loss or gradient.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L54-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b36a46cc010177414379aeee09d2f80cf856680eba2f204c2b6793ba56647574:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/__init__.py#L21-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d2e2875951e2fa2991980abb3dc2c9d18836e1a5ac925ac43991b03f6f3157ad:"
        },
